        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "0c75e5ca-7729-55dd-8937-fd0869ef4b42",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Han van Meegeren, Hermann Göring\n- Roles: painter, portraitist, art forger, political leader, military leader, fighter pilot ace\n- Organizations: Nazi Party (NSDAP)\n- Places: Netherlands, Germany\n- Events: World War I, Nazi Occupation of the Netherlands, World War II\n\nFacts:\n- Han van Meegeren was born on 10 October 1889 and died on 30 December 1947.\n- Hermann Göring was born on 12 January 1893 and died on 15 October 1946.\n- Han van Meegeren was a Dutch painter and portraitist who is considered one of the most ingenious art forgers of the 20th century.\n- Hermann Göring was a German political and military leader and one of the most powerful figures in the Nazi Party (NSDAP), which ruled Germany from 1933 to 1945.\n- Hermann Göring was a veteran World War I fighter pilot ace and received the Pour le Mérite.\n- After World War II, Han van Meegeren became a national hero because it was revealed that he had sold a forged painting to Hermann Göring during the Nazi Occupation of the Netherlands.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
